<title>SPAIN: Spain is suffering damages from truckers' strike.</title>
<headline>Spain is suffering damages from truckers' strike.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Development Minister Rafael Arias Salgado said on Friday that Spain will guarantee unimpeded travel on its roads despite a truckers' strike which is imposing grave damages on the economy.</p>
<p>&quot;This action is conducted by a radical minority which is aiming to harm the national economy...I want to say the government will guarantee unimpeded travel on Spanish road,&quot; said Salgado speaking to the weekly cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>He said also that the Spanish economy is suffering grave damages from the nine-day-old strike.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340  </p>
<p>&quot;This is a savage, violent and unjustified stoppage which is causing grave damages to the national economy,&quot; Salgado said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
